From 3cfeeb21d1f9c189acb99bff737c355a823edd5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:45:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 244/244] mir: call arguments are moved into the call only once
 all are lowered

get_args (the arguments of calls, tuples and arrays) marked each
argument's temporary moved as soon as it was lowered. A later argument
that exits early then skipped the earlier ones' drops:

    take2(D(x), return 1);              // D(x) leaked
    let t = (D(x), if e { return 9 } else { 10 });
    f(a.clone(), x?)                    // the clone leaked on the Err path

and one that awaits left them out of the coroutine state (C76):

    async fn temp_across() -> u32 { take2(make_guard(), yield_now().await) }

    MIR ERROR: <future#temp_across as Future>::poll BB18/TERM:
        ensure_valid: Use of non-valid lvalue - _5

The temporaries are now marked moved after the last argument is
lowered, just before the call (or the tuple/array) consumes them: an
early exit drops them like any other live temporary, and an await keeps
them, as rustc does (a non-Send argument held across an await now makes
the future non-Send there too). Struct literals and tuple struct /
variant constructors already consumed their operands at the end.

Found with the 0243 kit (diverging-operand-test). Kit
arg-temp-early-exit-test: early `return`/`break`/one-arm `if` after
a droppable argument of a function, a method, a tuple and an array (one
drop each), the normal path (no double drop), and the C76 future run to
completion and cancelled while suspended.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mir/from_hir.cpp | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mir/from_hir.cpp b/src/mir/from_hir.cpp
index b3eaca70..b79b1b0d 100644
--- a/src/mir/from_hir.cpp
+++ b/src/mir/from_hir.cpp
@@ -2440,10 +2440,16 @@ namespace {
                         values.push_back( mv$(tmp) );
                     }
                 }
-
-                if(const auto* e = values.back().opt_LValue() )
+            }
+            // The call/tuple/array consumes the argument temporaries, but only once all of them are lowered: marked
+            // moved one by one, an argument that exits early leaked the earlier ones (`f(a.clone(), x?)`, `(v, return
+            // ..)`: no drop on the early return), and one that awaits didn't keep them in the coroutine state ("Use
+            // of non-valid lvalue" after the resume)
+            for(size_t i = 0; i < values.size(); i ++)
+            {
+                if(const auto* e = values[i].opt_LValue() )
                 {
-                    m_builder.moved_lvalue( arg->span(), *e );
+                    m_builder.moved_lvalue( args[i]->span(), *e );
                 }
             }
             return values;
